Good morning team, and welcome to your weekly CSS update for the second week of October.
First, student governance is front and centre: voting in the Semester 1 Woroni Board Elections is open today and closes Thursday, October 15th at 5:00 pm. Please make sure your students cast their votes online.
On university policy, consultations are closing soon. Feedback on the Definitions for the new Anti-Racism Framework closed over the weekend, but you still have until Sunday, October 18th to submit anonymous feedback on the main Framework and Impacts papers. 
For our researchers and students, two major display opportunities have closing dates this week:
1.	Exhibitor registrations for our Semester 2 College Showcase close this Friday, October 16th.
2.	SoEN HDRs and Early Career Researchers have until Monday, October 19th to submit three-minute video or slide proposals for Pitch & Collaborate 2026.
Turning to funding and grants, applications close this Friday, October 16th for the 2026 ANU Hansen Scandinavian Friendship Endowment Grants. Up to $10,000 is available for research linkages and $5,000 for HDR travel. Looking further ahead, community groups and schools can apply for up to $2,500 via the ACT Youth Week Grants until November 10th.
In training and development, we have several key sessions this week:
•	Today at 2:30 pm, the Educational Fellowship Scheme is hosting an EFS Shut Up and Write session for academic staff.
•	Tomorrow, Wednesday October 14th, grab your bike for National Ride2Work Day starting in Dickson at 8:00 am, or tune into ANU Green's Commuting Essentials webinar on Teams at midday.
•	On Friday afternoon, October 16th, join us in the Birch Building Innovation Space from 1:00 to 3:00 pm for our workshop, 'From Ideas to Impact: Navigating Research Grants at ANU'.
Looking at events on campus, today is Ada Lovelace Day, celebrating women in STEM across campus. At 1:00 pm today, University House hosts an all-staff and student Community Meeting with Chancellor Gordon de Brouwer and Interim VC Rebekah Brown, with lunch provided.
Tomorrow at 11:15 am, President Surangel Whipps Jr. of Palau delivers a keynote on ocean protection and climate change. And this weekend, Chifley Meadows will come alive on Saturday, October 17th for the ANUSA After Hours Concert. Expect some noise and foot traffic around central precinct during setup.
 
Finally, a quick administrative reminder: while end-of-year cutoffs feel distant, SoEN Admin has set local procurement and order deadlines for November 2nd due to reduced team capacity later this semester. Please submit your purchasing requests early.
And a huge congratulations to our ANU Rocketry Team for taking out the overall title at the 2026 Australian Universities Rocketry Competition!

Have a productive week, everyone!
